body:
there ended up being three main directions
- dont care and copy the strings each time
- add flag and CharString field to StringName _Data to cache a utf8 string
- implement a utf8 internment class

Augmenting the StringName was the smaller change, but i dont imagine anyone would appreciate the additional fields and touching that class so I didnt look too much into it. kinda was looking like this:
```diff
diff --git a/core/string/string_name.h b/core/string/string_name.h
index bcb6407427..3177ad7d8e 100644
--- a/core/string/string_name.h
+++ b/core/string/string_name.h
@@ -44,6 +44,8 @@ class [[nodiscard]] StringName {
                SafeRefCount refcount;
                SafeNumeric<uint32_t> static_count;
                String name;
+               mutable CharString utf8_cache;  // Lazy: empty until first get_utf8()
+               mutable bool utf8_cached = false;
 #ifdef DEBUG_ENABLED
                uint32_t debug_references = 0;
 #endif
@@ -85,6 +87,14 @@ public:
        bool operator!=(const char *p_name) const;

        const char32_t *get_data() const { return _data ? _data->name.ptr() : U""; }
+       _FORCE_INLINE_ const char* get_utf8_data() const {
+               if (!_data) { return ""; }
+               if (!(_data->utf8_cached)) {
+                       _data->utf8_cache = _data->name.utf8();
+                       _data->utf8_cached = true;
+               }
+               return _data->utf8_cache.get_data();
+       }
        char32_t operator[](int p_index) const;
        int length() const;
        _FORCE_INLINE_ bool is_empty() const { return !_data; }
```


So i thought, I might try to copy the StringName class to get its internment properties how hard can it be?
took me a while, but I have it stripped down to something that i feel might work, I'll tidy up a bit and then update my PR.

I started to think that a generic internment template could be made, but thats more than i am bargaining for.
